 357:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/Tricore/Hssl/Hssl/IfxHssl_Hssl.h ****  * \subsection IfxLld_Hssl_Hssl_Interrupts Interrupts usage
 358:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/Tricore/Hssl/Hssl/IfxHssl_Hssl.h ****  *
 359:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/Tricore/Hssl/Hssl/IfxHssl_Hssl.h ****  * Interrupts can be enabled from the application by using the APIs provided in the driver,
 360:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/Tricore/Hssl/Hssl/IfxHssl_Hssl.h ****  * there are APIs available in the driver to enable, disable, clear and read the status of interrup
 361:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/Tricore/Hssl/Hssl/IfxHssl_Hssl.h ****  * APIs to enable the interrupts are also available.
 362:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/Tricore/Hssl/Hssl/IfxHssl_Hssl.h ****  *
 363:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/Tricore/Hssl/Hssl/IfxHssl_Hssl.h ****  * here is an example of how to use the interrupts in HSSL driver.
